MintToLiquidityHook::registerPool
├── When the adapter is the zero address
│   └── It should revert
├── When the caller is not the adapter's owner
│   └── It should revert
├── When the fee is dynamic
│   └── It should revert
├── When the token is native or equals the quote currency
│   └── It should revert
├── When the pool is already registered
│   └── It should revert
├── When the adapter's band is invalid
│   └── It should revert
└── When the inputs are valid
    ├── It should bind the pool to the adapter
    ├── It should initialise the pool at the band's midpoint
    └── It should emit PoolRegistered

MintToLiquidityHook::beforeInitialize
├── When the caller is not the PoolManager
│   └── It should revert
├── When the pool is not registered
│   └── It should revert
└── When the pool is registered
    └── It should let the pool initialise

MintToLiquidityHook::beforeSwap
├── When the caller is not the PoolManager
│   └── It should revert
├── Given the band is invalid or cannot be read
│   ├── It should emit BandInvalidated
│   └── It should leave the swap to the curve
├── Given the pool price is outside the band
│   ├── When the rebalance would carry the price to or past the swapper's limit
│   │   └── It should leave the rebalance to afterSwap
│   ├── When the rebalance reverts
│   │   ├── It should emit RebalanceSkipped
│   │   └── It should not revert the swap
│   └── When the rebalance succeeds
│       └── It should move the price to the band edge before the swap runs
├── Given the pool has no active liquidity
│   └── It should fill the swap from the issuer
├── Given the pool price is at the band edge the swap heads for
│   └── It should fill the swap from the issuer
├── Given the pool price is inside the band and the pool has liquidity
│   └── It should leave the swap to the curve
├── When the swapper's price limit does not allow the band edge
│   └── It should leave the swap to the curve
└── When the direct fill reverts
    ├── It should emit DirectFillSkipped
    └── It should leave the swap to the curve

MintToLiquidityHook::fillInternal
├── When the caller is not the hook
│   └── It should revert
├── When the swap is a buy
│   ├── When the input is exact
│   │   └── It should mint floor(quote / ceiling) tokens
│   ├── When the output is exact
│   │   ├── It should charge ceil(tokens * ceiling) quote
│   │   └── It should send surplus tokens to the beneficiary
│   └── When the PoolManager holds less quote than the swap needs
│       └── It should fill up to the PoolManager's reserves
└── When the swap is a sell
    ├── When the input is exact
    │   └── It should pay floor(tokens * floor) minus the rounding slack
    ├── When the output is exact
    │   └── It should charge ceil((quote + slack) / floor) tokens
    ├── When the swap is worth more than the issuer's exit capacity
    │   ├── It should fill up to the capacity
    │   └── It should round the tokens down so the redemption never exceeds the capacity
    ├── When the issuer has no exit capacity
    │   └── It should revert
    ├── When the PoolManager holds fewer tokens than the swap needs
    │   └── It should fill up to the PoolManager's reserves
    └── When the issuer pays one base unit less than tokens * floor
        └── It should still fill

MintToLiquidityHook::afterSwap
├── Given beforeSwap filled the whole swap
│   └── It should do nothing
├── Given the swap pushed the price past the ceiling
│   ├── It should mint at the ceiling and sell into the pool down to it
│   └── It should send the profit to the beneficiary
└── Given the swap pushed the price past the floor
    ├── It should buy from the pool up to the floor and redeem at it
    └── It should send the profit to the beneficiary

MintToLiquidityHook::rebalance
├── When the pool is not registered
│   └── It should revert
├── When the band is invalid
│   └── It should revert
├── Given the price is inside the band
│   └── It should return false
├── Given the price is above the ceiling
│   ├── When the pool has no liquidity
│   │   └── It should move the price to the ceiling without calling the issuer
│   ├── When selling down to the ceiling pays less than the mint costs
│   │   └── It should revert
│   ├── When the issuer reverts
│   │   └── It should revert
│   └── When the trade is profitable
│       ├── It should leave the price at the ceiling
│       └── It should send the profit to the beneficiary
└── Given the price is below the floor
    ├── When the issuer has no exit capacity
    │   └── It should revert
    ├── When the exit capacity is less than the trade needs
    │   └── It should buy what the capacity redeems and leave the price below the floor
    └── When the trade is profitable
        ├── It should leave the price at the floor
        └── It should send the profit to the beneficiary

MintToLiquidityHook::rebalanceInternal
└── When the caller is not the hook
    └── It should revert

MintToLiquidityHook::unlockCallback
└── When the caller is not the PoolManager
    └── It should revert
